### Send Email with React Email Template via CLI

Source: https://resend.com/docs/cli

Use the Resend CLI to send an email using a React Email template. Specify sender, recipient, subject, and the path to your template file.

```bash
resend emails send --from "Acme <onboarding@resend.dev>" --to delivered@resend.dev --subject "Hello World" --react-email ./emails/welcome.tsx
```

### Emails > Send an email

Source: https://resend.com/docs/llms-full.txt

The `resend emails send` command allows you to send an email. You can provide all options via flags for scripting or let the CLI prompt interactively for missing fields. Required flags include `--from`, `--to`, and `--subject`. You must also provide either `--text`, `--text-file`, `--html`, `--html-file`, or `--react-email` for the email body. The `--template` flag can be used with template variables to send pre-defined emails.

### Send Email with Template

Source: https://resend.com/docs/dashboard/templates/introduction

Use this to send an email using a pre-defined template ID and pass custom variables for personalization. Ensure the template exists in your Resend dashboard.

```javascript
await resend.emails.send({
  from: 'Acme <onboarding@resend.dev>',
  to: 'delivered@resend.dev',
  template: {
    id: 'order-confirmation',
    variables: {
      PRODUCT: 'Vintage Macintosh',
      PRICE: 499,
    },
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### Send Email with Template

Source: https://resend.com/docs/dashboard/templates/introduction

Send an email using a pre-defined template with specific variables. Ensure the template ID and variables are correctly configured.

```javascript
import { Resend } from 'resend';

const resend = new Resend('re_xxxxxxxxx');

await resend.emails.send({
  from: 'Acme <onboarding@resend.dev>',
  to: 'delivered@resend.dev',
  template: {
    id: 'order-confirmation',
    variables: {
      PRODUCT: 'Vintage Macintosh',
      PRICE: 499,
    },
  },
});

```

