### Send Email with Template and Variables (Node.js)

Source: https://resend.com/docs/llms-full.txt

Use this snippet to send a transactional email using a published template ID and provide specific variable values for personalization. Ensure the Resend library is installed and initialized with your API key.

```typescript
import { Resend } from 'resend';

const resend = new Resend('re_xxxxxxxxx');

const { data, error } = await resend.emails.send({
  from: 'Acme <onboarding@resend.dev>',
  to: ['delivered@resend.dev'],
  subject: 'hello world',
  template: {
    id: 'f3b9756c-f4f4-44da-bc00-9f7903c8a83f',
    variables: {
      PRODUCT: 'Laptop',
    },
  },
});
```

### Send Batch Emails > Body Parameters > template

Source: https://resend.com/docs/api-reference/emails/send-batch-emails

To send emails using a template, provide a 'template' object with an 'id' (or alias) and optionally 'variables'. If a template is used, 'html', 'text', or 'react' cannot be included in the payload. The 'from', 'subject', and 'reply_to' fields in the payload take precedence over the template's defaults.

--------------------------------

### Emails > Send Email > Template

Source: https://resend.com/docs/api-reference/emails/send-email

Emails can be sent using pre-defined templates by providing a template ID or alias and an object for variables. When using a template, you cannot simultaneously provide HTML, text, or React content. The 'from', 'subject', and 'reply_to' fields in the payload will override the template's defaults if provided.
